If #5592 refactoring is added then instead of having `txFeaturesMap_` as {transaction name:list of features}, it can be {transaction name:function}. Where the function is a specific transactor's `isEnabled()`. `isEnabled()` probably would have to be overloaded to take `Rules`.

    std::unordered_map<std::uint16_t, std::function<bool(Rules const&)>> txFeaturesMap_;

and then in Permission.cpp you can build a map of transaction name to a function and there is no need to change `transactions.macro`. `isDelegatable()` instead of checking if a feature is enabled, calls `isEnabled()` of a specific transactor. I think this should work.

